==Skills and Abilities==
As the only storm dragon in the game, Mulaamnir possesses unique capabilities, including his ability to summon [[ON:Storm Wyrm|storm wyrms]] and [[ON:Storm Atronach|storm atronachs]] during combat. Also, due to his high amount of health, the only effective way of depleting it is through the use of the Dragonhorn.

;Bite: A melee attack that causes bleeding.
;Shocking Bite: The dragon bites you with its mouth charged with its elemental energy, dealing high shock damage. This can be blocked.
;Tail Smash: If standing behind the dragon, it slams the ground with its tail, dealing high physical damage and knocking you away.
;Sweeping Breath: The dragon breathes its element in front of himself, indicated by a moving conical AoE, dealing high shock damage.
;Storm Aura: A constant AoE that surrounds the underside of the dragon, causing shock damage if entered.
;Wing Thrash: A melee attack where the dragon slashes targets on its side with its wing. In the case of Mulaamnir, it also releases three gusts of electrically-charged wind, indicated by traveling AoEs, dealing high shock damage and snaring you.
;Lightning Breath: A flight-based attack where an airborne dragon flies over and breathes lightning in a straight line, lingering for a long time. In the case of Mulaamnir, on the third fly-by, the area will be in the shape of a half-circle and after all of his fly-byes, [[ON:Storm Wyrm|Storm Wyrms]] are summoned.
;Storm Trail: The left-over lightning from a lightning breath attack. It doesn't have an AoE indicator.
;Bombardment: While flying, Mulaamnir pelts the arena with lightning bolts, indicated by circular AoEs, dealing moderate lightning damage and staggering you.
;Moon Blast: Kaalgrontiid empowers Mulaamnir, allowing him to shoot a ray of lunar energy that can only be avoided by using Abnur Tharn's shield, otherwise it deals lethal damage.
;Crash: After Mulaamnir uses Moon Blast, you need to use the Dragonhorn to damage him greatly. After feeling the effect of the horn, Mulaamnir crashes down from his perch and if you are in the landing area, you are knocked far away.
;Summon Atronach: After the first use of the horn, Mulaamnir summons a [[ON:Storm Atronach|Storm Atronach]] in the arena and after the second, an [[ON:Air Atronach|Air Atronach]].

